1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,212
Sweetheart, after Christmas,

2
00:00:02,212 --> 00:00:05,293
every refrigerator in America has a ham

3
00:00:05,293 --> 00:00:06,794
bone sitting in it,

4
00:00:06,794 --> 00:00:08,058
wrapped in foil,

5
00:00:08,058 --> 00:00:10,112
waiting to be thrown away.

6
00:00:10,292 --> 00:00:12,939
Don't you dare throw it away.

7
00:00:13,119 --> 00:00:15,490
That bone is worth more than the

8
00:00:15,490 --> 00:00:16,230
whole ham.

9
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:18,875
It makes the best soup you'll ever

10
00:00:18,875 --> 00:00:20,397
eat, thick and smoky,

11
00:00:20,397 --> 00:00:22,136
for about three dollars,

12
00:00:22,136 --> 00:00:24,166
enough to feed eight people.

13
00:00:24,346 --> 00:00:27,314
But most people's bean soup comes out

14
00:00:27,314 --> 00:00:30,201
thin, bland, and with beans that are

15
00:00:30,201 --> 00:00:31,405
hard as gravel.

16
00:00:31,755 --> 00:00:34,463
So tonight I'm giving you my mother's

17
00:00:34,463 --> 00:00:35,780
ham and bean soup,

18
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:36,732
step by step,

19
00:00:36,732 --> 00:00:39,220
the way she made it every December

20
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:40,172
twenty-sixth.

21
00:00:40,352 --> 00:00:42,964
And the five mistakes that ruin it.

22
00:00:43,144 --> 00:00:44,040
Stay with me,

23
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:46,589
because the last secret is the reason

24
00:00:46,589 --> 00:00:48,794
her soup was so thick and creamy

25
00:00:48,794 --> 00:00:50,447
without a drop of cream,

26
00:00:50,447 --> 00:00:52,583
and it takes about ten seconds.

27
00:00:52,933 --> 00:00:53,941
In our house,

28
00:00:53,941 --> 00:00:56,810
the day after Christmas was soup day.

29
00:00:56,990 --> 00:00:59,582
My mother would take the bone from

30
00:00:59,582 --> 00:01:00,954
the Christmas ham,

31
00:01:00,954 --> 00:01:03,393
put it in her biggest pot before

32
00:01:03,393 --> 00:01:04,765
anybody was awake,

33
00:01:04,765 --> 00:01:05,755
and by lunch,

34
00:01:05,755 --> 00:01:08,728
the whole house smelled smoky and warm.

35
00:01:08,908 --> 00:01:10,838
We'd eat it with cornbread,

36
00:01:10,838 --> 00:01:13,626
sitting around the kitchen table in our

37
00:01:13,626 --> 00:01:15,271
new Christmas sweaters,

38
00:01:15,271 --> 00:01:17,845
and nobody had to cook anything else

39
00:01:17,845 --> 00:01:18,417
all day.

40
00:01:18,767 --> 00:01:21,585
Ham and beans was poor folks' food

41
00:01:21,585 --> 00:01:23,575
for three hundred years,

42
00:01:23,575 --> 00:01:24,072
honey.

43
00:01:24,252 --> 00:01:25,460
In the old days,

44
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,648
a family would eat the ham at

45
00:01:27,648 --> 00:01:29,158
Christmas or Easter,

46
00:01:29,158 --> 00:01:31,723
and then that bone would feed them

47
00:01:31,723 --> 00:01:33,006
for another week.

48
00:01:33,186 --> 00:01:34,754
Beans were cheap.

49
00:01:34,934 --> 00:01:36,454
Onions were cheap.

50
00:01:36,634 --> 00:01:38,840
And a ham bone was free.

51
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:40,890
In a minute I'll tell you how

52
00:01:40,890 --> 00:01:42,502
to get a ham bone even if

53
00:01:42,502 --> 00:01:43,920
you didn't make a ham.

54
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:46,991
In the Senate dining room in Washington,

55
00:01:46,991 --> 00:01:49,439
they've served bean soup made with a

56
00:01:49,439 --> 00:01:51,820
ham bone every single day since the

57
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:53,453
early nineteen hundreds.

58
00:01:53,633 --> 00:01:54,817
It's a rule.

59
00:01:54,997 --> 00:01:58,387
Senators, presidents, every one of them.

60
00:01:58,567 --> 00:02:00,483
My father loved that.

61
00:02:00,663 --> 00:02:02,078
He'd say, Dorothy,

62
00:02:02,078 --> 00:02:04,750
we're eating like a senator today.

63
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:07,066
And my mother would say,

64
00:02:07,066 --> 00:02:10,359
Walter, a senator never ate soup this

65
00:02:10,359 --> 00:02:10,804
good.

66
00:02:11,155 --> 00:02:12,710
Here's what you need.

67
00:02:12,890 --> 00:02:14,475
One meaty ham bone,

68
00:02:14,475 --> 00:02:16,478
or two smoked ham hocks.

69
00:02:16,658 --> 00:02:19,286
One pound of dried navy beans or

70
00:02:19,286 --> 00:02:21,011
great northern beans.

71
00:02:21,191 --> 00:02:22,390
One big onion,

72
00:02:22,390 --> 00:02:25,644
two carrots, and two stalks of celery,

73
00:02:25,644 --> 00:02:26,671
all chopped.

74
00:02:26,851 --> 00:02:28,883
Three cloves of garlic.

75
00:02:29,063 --> 00:02:30,433
Two bay leaves.

76
00:02:30,613 --> 00:02:33,167
A teaspoon of dried thyme.

77
00:02:33,347 --> 00:02:35,971
Ten cups of water or chicken broth.

78
00:02:36,151 --> 00:02:37,788
And black pepper.

79
00:02:37,968 --> 00:02:39,570
Don't add salt yet.

80
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:41,376
I'll tell you why.

81
00:02:41,726 --> 00:02:43,861
And if you don't have a ham

82
00:02:43,861 --> 00:02:46,787
bone, honey, buy two smoked ham hocks

83
00:02:46,787 --> 00:02:49,475
at the meat counter for about four

84
00:02:49,475 --> 00:02:50,108
dollars.

85
00:02:50,288 --> 00:02:51,902
Or ask the butcher.

86
00:02:52,082 --> 00:02:55,001
Most grocery stores that sell spiral hams

87
00:02:55,001 --> 00:02:57,351
will give you the bone for almost

88
00:02:57,351 --> 00:02:59,059
nothing after Christmas.

89
00:02:59,239 --> 00:03:01,141
The ham hock has all the smoke

90
00:03:01,141 --> 00:03:02,345
and all the flavor,

91
00:03:02,345 --> 00:03:04,499
and the skin and gristle melt into

92
00:03:04,499 --> 00:03:06,147
the soup and make it rich.

93
00:03:06,498 --> 00:03:08,018
Mistake number one.

94
00:03:08,198 --> 00:03:10,195
Not soaking the beans.

95
00:03:10,375 --> 00:03:12,287
Put the dry beans in a big

96
00:03:12,287 --> 00:03:14,861
bowl, pick out any little stones or

97
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:17,802
shriveled ones, and cover them with cold

98
00:03:17,802 --> 00:03:19,420
water by three inches.

99
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,248
Leave them overnight.

100
00:03:21,428 --> 00:03:23,402
They'll double in size.

101
00:03:23,582 --> 00:03:24,737
In the morning,

102
00:03:24,737 --> 00:03:26,740
drain them and rinse them.

103
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:29,857
Soaked beans cook evenly and they're much

104
00:03:29,857 --> 00:03:31,505
easier on your stomach,

105
00:03:31,505 --> 00:03:33,224
if you know what I mean.

106
00:03:33,574 --> 00:03:35,106
Forgot to soak them?

107
00:03:35,286 --> 00:03:37,480
Here's my mother's quick soak.

108
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:39,324
Put the beans in a pot,

109
00:03:39,324 --> 00:03:40,916
cover them with water,

110
00:03:40,916 --> 00:03:42,797
bring it to a boil for two

111
00:03:42,797 --> 00:03:45,329
minutes, then turn off the heat and

112
00:03:45,329 --> 00:03:47,355
let them sit with the lid on

113
00:03:47,355 --> 00:03:48,295
for one hour.

114
00:03:48,475 --> 00:03:50,205
Drain and rinse.

115
00:03:50,385 --> 00:03:52,591
It works almost as well.

116
00:03:52,771 --> 00:03:56,032
And mistake number two is using old

117
00:03:56,032 --> 00:03:56,591
beans.

118
00:03:56,771 --> 00:03:58,851
If that bag has been in your

119
00:03:58,851 --> 00:04:00,560
pantry for three years,

120
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,343
they may never get soft.

121
00:04:02,694 --> 00:04:04,510
If this is helping you,

122
00:04:04,510 --> 00:04:06,643
tap the like button for me,

123
00:04:06,643 --> 00:04:07,512
sweetheart.

124
00:04:07,692 --> 00:04:10,385
It helps Grandma more than you know.

125
00:04:10,565 --> 00:04:12,826
Put the ham bone in your biggest

126
00:04:12,826 --> 00:04:14,733
pot with the drained beans,

127
00:04:14,733 --> 00:04:15,792
the bay leaves,

128
00:04:15,792 --> 00:04:17,911
the thyme, and the ten cups of

129
00:04:17,911 --> 00:04:18,971
water or broth.

130
00:04:19,151 --> 00:04:20,541
Bring it to a boil,

131
00:04:20,541 --> 00:04:22,663
then turn it down to a gentle

132
00:04:22,663 --> 00:04:24,712
simmer, with the lid tilted.

133
00:04:24,892 --> 00:04:26,839
Let it go for about an hour

134
00:04:26,839 --> 00:04:27,632
and a half.

135
00:04:27,982 --> 00:04:30,304
Now, mistake number three.

136
00:04:30,484 --> 00:04:32,480
Adding salt at the beginning.

137
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:34,790
The ham is already salty,

138
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:37,091
and as the soup cooks down,

139
00:04:37,091 --> 00:04:38,454
it gets saltier.

140
00:04:38,634 --> 00:04:40,090
If you salt it now,

141
00:04:40,090 --> 00:04:43,615
it'll be like drinking seawater by dinnertime.

142
00:04:43,795 --> 00:04:46,464
And old cooks say salt early makes

143
00:04:46,464 --> 00:04:48,113
the bean skins tough.

144
00:04:48,293 --> 00:04:50,445
Wait until the very end,

145
00:04:50,445 --> 00:04:52,775
taste it, and then decide.

146
00:04:52,955 --> 00:04:54,336
Most of the time,

147
00:04:54,336 --> 00:04:56,531
it doesn't need any at all.

148
00:04:56,881 --> 00:04:58,564
Mistake number four.

149
00:04:58,744 --> 00:05:01,530
Adding tomatoes or vinegar too early.

150
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:04,381
Acid keeps beans from softening.

151
00:05:04,561 --> 00:05:06,870
If you like tomatoes in your bean

152
00:05:06,870 --> 00:05:08,619
soup, and some people do,

153
00:05:08,619 --> 00:05:10,929
add them only after the beans are

154
00:05:10,929 --> 00:05:12,188
completely tender.

155
00:05:12,368 --> 00:05:14,422
My Aunt Louise put a can of

156
00:05:14,422 --> 00:05:17,311
tomatoes in at the beginning one year,

157
00:05:17,311 --> 00:05:20,125
and those beans were still crunchy at

158
00:05:20,125 --> 00:05:20,809
midnight.

159
00:05:20,989 --> 00:05:23,392
My mother never let her forget it.

160
00:05:23,743 --> 00:05:25,875
After an hour and a half,

161
00:05:25,875 --> 00:05:27,751
add the chopped onion,

162
00:05:27,751 --> 00:05:30,140
carrots, celery, and garlic.

163
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:32,555
Simmer another forty-five minutes,

164
00:05:32,555 --> 00:05:34,790
until the beans are creamy all the

165
00:05:34,790 --> 00:05:35,579
way through.

166
00:05:35,759 --> 00:05:38,489
Test one by squeezing it between your

167
00:05:38,489 --> 00:05:39,079
fingers.

168
00:05:39,259 --> 00:05:41,807
If it smashes easily with no hard

169
00:05:41,807 --> 00:05:43,427
center, they're done.

170
00:05:43,607 --> 00:05:45,377
If it fights you,

171
00:05:45,377 --> 00:05:46,521
keep going.

172
00:05:46,701 --> 00:05:49,263
Beans take as long as they take,

173
00:05:49,263 --> 00:05:49,743
honey.

174
00:05:50,094 --> 00:05:52,202
And if you're short on time,

175
00:05:52,202 --> 00:05:54,612
sweetheart, you can make it in a

176
00:05:54,612 --> 00:05:55,515
slow cooker.

177
00:05:55,695 --> 00:05:57,194
Put the soaked beans,

178
00:05:57,194 --> 00:05:58,121
the ham bone,

179
00:05:58,121 --> 00:06:00,904
the herbs, the vegetables and the water

180
00:06:00,904 --> 00:06:01,974
all in at once,

181
00:06:01,974 --> 00:06:03,972
and cook it on low for eight

182
00:06:03,972 --> 00:06:06,469
to nine hours while you're at work.

183
00:06:06,649 --> 00:06:08,704
It comes out just as good.

184
00:06:08,884 --> 00:06:11,471
Just don't use the quick soak for

185
00:06:11,471 --> 00:06:12,724
the slow cooker,

186
00:06:12,724 --> 00:06:14,840
and don't skip the soaking.

187
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:17,897
Dry beans in a slow cooker sometimes

188
00:06:17,897 --> 00:06:19,095
never get soft.

189
00:06:19,446 --> 00:06:21,319
Now take out the ham bone and

190
00:06:21,319 --> 00:06:22,998
put it on a cutting board.

191
00:06:23,178 --> 00:06:25,316
Let it cool for a few minutes,

192
00:06:25,316 --> 00:06:27,524
then pull off every bit of meat

193
00:06:27,524 --> 00:06:29,448
with a fork and chop it up.

194
00:06:29,628 --> 00:06:31,006
Throw away the bone,

195
00:06:31,006 --> 00:06:32,798
the skin, and the gristle,

196
00:06:32,798 --> 00:06:34,727
and put the meat back in the

197
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:35,003
pot.

198
00:06:35,183 --> 00:06:37,668
And fish out those bay leaves.

199
00:06:37,848 --> 00:06:40,177
My father bit into one once and

200
00:06:40,177 --> 00:06:41,981
said he'd been poisoned.

201
00:06:42,331 --> 00:06:44,659
Now the secret I promised you,

202
00:06:44,659 --> 00:06:46,290
the ten-second trick.

203
00:06:46,470 --> 00:06:49,151
Mistake number five is thin,

204
00:06:49,151 --> 00:06:50,301
watery soup.

205
00:06:50,481 --> 00:06:52,669
Take two cups of the beans out

206
00:06:52,669 --> 00:06:53,617
with a ladle,

207
00:06:53,617 --> 00:06:55,003
put them in a bowl,

208
00:06:55,003 --> 00:06:57,483
and mash them with a potato masher

209
00:06:57,483 --> 00:07:00,036
or a fork until they're like paste.

210
00:07:00,216 --> 00:07:02,224
Stir them back into the pot.

211
00:07:02,404 --> 00:07:03,518
In two minutes,

212
00:07:03,518 --> 00:07:06,266
the whole soup turns thick and creamy

213
00:07:06,266 --> 00:07:08,642
and rich, like there's a pint of

214
00:07:08,642 --> 00:07:09,533
cream in it.

215
00:07:09,713 --> 00:07:11,257
And there's not a drop.

216
00:07:11,607 --> 00:07:13,192
And then taste it,

217
00:07:13,192 --> 00:07:14,161
sweetheart.

218
00:07:14,341 --> 00:07:16,782
Now add salt if it needs it,

219
00:07:16,782 --> 00:07:19,136
and plenty of black pepper.

220
00:07:19,316 --> 00:07:21,413
And here's a little extra that my

221
00:07:21,413 --> 00:07:24,273
mother learned from a neighbor from Kentucky.

222
00:07:24,453 --> 00:07:27,124
A splash of cider vinegar right at

223
00:07:27,124 --> 00:07:29,167
the end, about a teaspoon.

224
00:07:29,347 --> 00:07:32,185
It makes the whole soup taste brighter

225
00:07:32,185 --> 00:07:34,351
and smokier at the same time.

226
00:07:34,531 --> 00:07:36,667
Taste before and after.

227
00:07:36,847 --> 00:07:38,205
You won't believe it.

228
00:07:38,556 --> 00:07:40,146
And give it time.

229
00:07:40,326 --> 00:07:41,867
Like every bean soup,

230
00:07:41,867 --> 00:07:43,702
it's better the next day,

231
00:07:43,702 --> 00:07:46,196
after the flavors have had a night

232
00:07:46,196 --> 00:07:47,884
together in the icebox.

233
00:07:48,064 --> 00:07:50,215
It thickens a lot overnight,

234
00:07:50,215 --> 00:07:52,519
so add a little water or broth

235
00:07:52,519 --> 00:07:54,055
when you warm it up.

236
00:07:54,235 --> 00:07:56,598
It keeps five days in the icebox

237
00:07:56,598 --> 00:07:58,960
and three months in the freezer.

238
00:07:59,140 --> 00:08:01,014
I freeze it in quart jars,

239
00:08:01,014 --> 00:08:03,680
and it's a winter's worth of lunches.

240
00:08:04,030 --> 00:08:06,776
Here's a trick for a smokier soup,

241
00:08:06,776 --> 00:08:09,845
honey, when your ham bone doesn't have

242
00:08:09,845 --> 00:08:11,541
much meat left on it.

243
00:08:11,721 --> 00:08:14,299
Brown a few slices of chopped bacon

244
00:08:14,299 --> 00:08:15,551
in the pot first,

245
00:08:15,551 --> 00:08:16,582
take them out,

246
00:08:16,582 --> 00:08:19,012
and cook your onions in the bacon

247
00:08:19,012 --> 00:08:21,810
grease before you add everything else.

248
00:08:21,990 --> 00:08:24,368
Then stir the crispy bacon in at

249
00:08:24,368 --> 00:08:24,962
the end.

250
00:08:25,142 --> 00:08:27,504
My son-in-law does it that way,

251
00:08:27,504 --> 00:08:29,485
and I'll admit he's right.

252
00:08:29,835 --> 00:08:31,846
Serve it in big bowls with a

253
00:08:31,846 --> 00:08:33,282
square of cornbread,

254
00:08:33,282 --> 00:08:34,072
sweetheart.

255
00:08:34,252 --> 00:08:35,881
In Ohio and Kentucky,

256
00:08:35,881 --> 00:08:38,750
a lot of people crumble the cornbread

257
00:08:38,750 --> 00:08:40,301
right into the soup.

258
00:08:40,481 --> 00:08:43,063
Some put a little chopped raw onion

259
00:08:43,063 --> 00:08:45,276
on top, which my father loved.

260
00:08:45,456 --> 00:08:47,463
And a bottle of hot sauce on

261
00:08:47,463 --> 00:08:49,972
the table for anybody who wants it.

262
00:08:50,152 --> 00:08:51,418
Nothing else.

263
00:08:51,598 --> 00:08:53,059
That's a whole meal,

264
00:08:53,059 --> 00:08:55,835
and it'll keep you warm all afternoon.

265
00:08:56,186 --> 00:08:58,294
When my children were little,

266
00:08:58,294 --> 00:09:00,039
the day after Christmas,

267
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:01,857
I'd make a pot of ham and

268
00:09:01,857 --> 00:09:04,257
bean soup and a pan of cornbread,

269
00:09:04,257 --> 00:09:06,366
and we'd take a big bowl next

270
00:09:06,366 --> 00:09:07,238
door to Mrs.

271
00:09:07,418 --> 00:09:10,623
Kowalski, who lived alone.

272
00:09:10,803 --> 00:09:13,043
And then we'd all go sledding.

273
00:09:13,223 --> 00:09:15,572
It's still my favorite day of the

274
00:09:15,572 --> 00:09:17,208
whole Christmas season,

275
00:09:17,208 --> 00:09:17,635
honey.

276
00:09:17,815 --> 00:09:19,754
Quieter than Christmas.

277
00:09:19,934 --> 00:09:21,292
No presents.

278
00:09:21,472 --> 00:09:23,417
Just soup, and snow,

279
00:09:23,417 --> 00:09:25,362
and people you love.

280
00:09:25,712 --> 00:09:27,105
So one more time.

281
00:09:27,285 --> 00:09:28,855
Save the ham bone,

282
00:09:28,855 --> 00:09:30,686
or buy a smoked hock.

283
00:09:30,866 --> 00:09:32,236
Soak your beans,

284
00:09:32,236 --> 00:09:33,862
and use fresh ones.

285
00:09:34,042 --> 00:09:36,259
Simmer them gently with the bone.

286
00:09:36,439 --> 00:09:39,556
No salt and no tomatoes until the

287
00:09:39,556 --> 00:09:39,934
end.

288
00:09:40,114 --> 00:09:42,064
Add the vegetables later.

289
00:09:42,244 --> 00:09:43,626
Pull off the ham.

290
00:09:43,806 --> 00:09:46,366
Mash two cups of beans and stir

291
00:09:46,366 --> 00:09:47,440
them back in.

292
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:49,315
And a splash of vinegar.

293
00:09:49,495 --> 00:09:51,110
That's my mother's soup,

294
00:09:51,110 --> 00:09:53,399
and it's the best thing you'll eat

295
00:09:53,399 --> 00:09:54,139
all winter.

296
00:09:54,489 --> 00:09:56,431
Tell me in the comments,

297
00:09:56,431 --> 00:09:57,321
sweetheart.

298
00:09:57,501 --> 00:09:59,209
Cornbread in your soup,

299
00:09:59,209 --> 00:10:00,323
or on the side?

300
00:10:00,503 --> 00:10:02,817
I want to know which team you're

301
00:10:02,817 --> 00:10:03,034
on.

302
00:10:03,214 --> 00:10:06,395
The whole playlist of Grandma's recipes is

303
00:10:06,395 --> 00:10:08,440
right there on your screen,

304
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:10,561
and I'll see you in the next

305
00:10:10,561 --> 00:10:11,016
video.

306
00:10:11,196 --> 00:10:12,833
Good night, honey.
